  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Barbus jae is one of the smallest species of barb from Africa. B. jae becomes only 2-3 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Sadly nowadays imports from Cameroon are very rare, so one has to be really lucky to find this jewel in a local pet shop.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>It has been described from the river Dja in Cameroon.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>This small fish is found in forest-streams.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>One should keep this fish at temperatures of about 20-22°C. Other water parameters are of minor interest.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>The males of B. jae are polychromatic. This means that each male has an individual coloration.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_jae_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding B. jae is not complicated, but not economical, so the species is not bred by professional breeders.</p>"
    },
    {
